## Finding

`pkix-path/tests/pkits_helper.rs:39`:

```rust
pub fn pkits_cert(name: &str) -> Certificate { ... }
```

Function panics (via `.unwrap_or_else(|| panic!(...))` for missing fixtures, and `Certificate::from_der(...).expect(...)` for parse failures) but has no `# Panics` doc section. Clippy: `clippy::missing_panics_doc`.

## Context

Test helper. Panicking for missing fixtures is the desired behavior — the test should fail loudly if the test corpus is missing. The lint just wants this documented.

## Fix

```rust
/// Load and parse a PKITS certificate fixture by name.
///
/// # Panics
///
/// Panics if the named fixture file does not exist or fails to parse as DER.
/// Tests using this helper should ensure the PKITS test corpus has been
/// extracted to `pkix-path/tests/pkits/`.
pub fn pkits_cert(name: &str) -> Certificate { ... }
```

## Priority

P4 — test helper doc nit.
